---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE_DESCRIPTION, SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
---

<BaseLayout title={SITE_TITLE} description={SITE_DESCRIPTION}>
	<h1>So, who am I?</h1>

	<p>
		I'm a senior engineer, 11+ years into platform engineering and distributed systems, mostly
		inside regulated financial and public-sector environments. I design and run the common
		infrastructure other teams build on - multi-tenant cloud foundations, GitOps self-service,
		secure data layers, the kind of systems that have to hold up under regulatory scrutiny and
		not just a demo.
	</p>

	<p>
		Most of what I write about these days lives at the intersection of that and AI-native
		development. <a href="https://github.com/m-stepkowski/kubemend">kubemend</a> is an LLM agent
		harness for Kubernetes remediation, hand-written with no agent frameworks, that diagnoses
		incidents from live cluster state and can only act by opening draft pull requests - a
		verification pipeline the model doesn't control re-checks every change before it's ever
		called "done." I've written up what building it actually taught me - costs, bugs, an
		adversarial prompt-injection test - in <a href="/blog">a short series of articles</a>.
	</p>

	<p>
		Outside of platform work I like building things end-to-end on my own. <a
			href="https://getrnkd.app">Rnkd</a
		> is a consumer product I shipped solo - design, mobile frontend, backend, infrastructure,
		distribution - and <a href="https://github.com/m-stepkowski/rgw-model">rgw-model</a> is a
		multi-agent reinforcement-learning environment, closer to my background in an MSc on
		multi-agent RL. Both, and a few other things, are on <a href="/projects">the projects page</a
		>.
	</p>

	<p>
		I'm a <a href="https://www.cncf.io/training/kubestronaut/">Kubestronaut</a> (all five CNCF
		Kubernetes certifications) and an AWS Certified Solutions Architect - Professional.
	</p>

	<p>
		You can find more of my code on <a href="https://github.com/m-stepkowski">GitHub</a>, or say
		hello on <a href="https://linkedin.com/in/maciej-stepkowski">LinkedIn</a> or <a
			href="https://x.com/mstepkowski">X</a
		>.
	</p>
</BaseLayout>
